  <h2>Structure first. AI second.</h2>
  <p>
    Asking AI to “build a website” without a keyword plan and a conversion framework is how you get
    pretty pages that don’t rank or convert. We decide which terms you can win, how each page is
    ordered, and what the hero must say, then AI accelerates production inside those rules. That’s
    the difference between a brochure and a lead system.
  </p>
  <p>
    For local trades we lean on Google Keyword Planner for volume (it’s the data source that matches
    real search behavior). Broad SEO tools built for huge content sites often invent local volumes.
    Service and city pages follow the same discipline: clear titles/H1s, light geographic relevance,
    and internal links that point strength back to the main page.
  </p>

  <h2>The homepage checklist (what most visitors actually see)</h2>
  <p>
    Roughly four in five visitors never scroll far. So the top of the page carries the sale: clarity,
    proof, and an obvious next step. Lower sections tick remaining objections for the people who need
    them, services, areas, process, risks of waiting or hiring wrong, FAQ, and another CTA. We
    document the full client-site pattern in our site structure &amp; SEO guide so builds stay
    consistent across companies.
  </p>
